  "chitchat": [
    "walks the gantry six inches to the left and stops it dead.",
    "\"Eleven years. Not one drop. You want to hear about the twelfth?\"",
    "\"When I shout MOVING, the correct response is moving.\""
  ],
  "description": "The gantry operator, who spends his shift standing very still with a pendant control in both hands, walking half a tonne of steel over people's heads at the speed of a slow apology. He has dropped nothing in eleven years and mentions this exactly as often as it comes up, which is constantly.",
  "dialogue_tree": {
    "bye": {
      "options": [],
      "text": "\"Right.\" The load comes down without a sound, and he takes up the slack for the next one."
    },
    "root": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "I'll wait.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Endacott does not take his eyes off the load. \"Talk if you like. I will answer when this is on the deck and not before.\""
    }
  },
